# Project Structure Standards

> file_patterns: ["*"]
> description: Guidelines for organizing project structure and dependencies

## Directory Organization
Standards for directory structure:
- Separate source code, tests, docs, and configs
- Use README.md for functionality documentation
- Store architecture diagrams in diagrams/
- Avoid excessive directory nesting

## Dependency Management
Guidelines for managing project dependencies:
- Use venv for virtual environment management (.venv directory)
- Use .env for configuration and secrets
- Use .gitignore for version control management
- Follow dependency injection principles

## Project Layout

### Required Files
> required: true

- README.md
- requirements.txt
- .env.example
- .gitignore

### Required Directories
> required: true

- src/
- tests/
- docs/
- config/

## Best Practices
- Keep project structure clean and logical
- Isolate dependencies properly
- Separate configuration from code
- Document directory structure in README

## File Organization
- Group related files together
- Use clear and consistent naming
- Keep directory depth reasonable
- Include necessary __init__.py files

## Configuration Management
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Keep secrets separate from code
- Document all configuration options
- Provide example configurations

## Version Control
- Use meaningful .gitignore rules
- Keep sensitive data out of version control
- Document branching strategy
- Include contribution guidelines 